<!-- Below are the commands to create the migrations -->
 
1.Creates a new migration script (also called a "revision") in your alembic/versions/ folder.The file gets a unique revision ID
 
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "create admins table"
 
 
2.Applies (runs) all pending migrations in the correct order — from the current database state up to the latest revision (called head).

alembic upgrade head